Both emit two NOPs before ordinary's function symbol and two after it;
local_override has one before and two after; notrace_entry has none and
no patch-table entry. The nonleaf aligned_entry places the two entry NOPs
before PACIASP and its frame setup, with CFI beginning at the function label.
The existing O0/O2 table/relocation probe is retained at
.evidence/builtin-probes/20260914-function-entry/oracles.out.

Important alignment interaction: both controls align the patch-region start,
not the callable symbol, to the explicit 64-byte alignment. The linked
aligned_entry addresses are GCC 0x948 and Clang 0x8c8, each 8 modulo 64.
This is not evidence that the function symbol is 64-byte aligned; it must be
reconciled explicitly with EvoIR's existing function-alignment contract before
implementing their combined mode. No general alignment rule is changed here.

