GCC14 -O2 -fmin-function-alignment=N emits .align 2/3/7 for N=4/8/128.
Clang19 rejects this GCC option spelling; its source-option run is NOT PASS.
GCC14's observed N=65 uses .align 6, contrary to the manual's next-power-of-two
description; EvoCC deliberately refuses non-power-of-two requests rather
than making a new rounding choice. The recorded kernel uses N=8.

